            "review_title": "Review at Pho Tu Hung",
            "review_text": "JSTrip_77\nSarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina1194 contributions\n0\nLegit Pho\nJan 2019 • Solo\nThis pho restaurant has attracted me for some time but I didn't try it until today. It's pretty much common knowledge that the best places are the places crowded with locals. There are always loads of motor bikes parked in front of this place. So - I went for it today. I had my normal beef pho with a mixture of beef brisket and blanched (rare) beef. This broth was absolutely one of the best that I've had yet. And, the portion of meat seemed larger than at some of the places I've tried recently which shocked me because the prices were actually lower. \n\nThis place was filled with older men which is a good indicator that it's good. But, it's also an indicator that they will soon be smoking. They did. That might be the only reason that I don't stop by more often. I just cannot stand the smoke-filled restaurants. This was the first time it really bothered me. Ironically, it probably bothered me more because this is actually a restaurant with real chairs and adult-level tables. That also means that it was less ventilated.\n\nSo, there you have it. Delicious food. Smoky environment. But the staff was friendly especially when I ordered in Vietnamese!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 18, 2019",
